    "exercise_name": "TIGHT QUEUE — Overlapping Raid, Three Unresolved",
    "situation_brief": "You are the console operator of a single ground-based air-defence site under a declared air-raid warning. Your radar does not rotate: it holds a fixed 120-degree sector centred on 045 degrees, and you are blind outside it. Detection range varies by target class — long for fast fixed-wing, shorter for rotary-wing, shortest for small unmanned tracks — and you may adjust tilt in elevation to place coverage where it is needed. Engagement rings are 70 km long range, 50 km medium, 20 km short, with a 5 km inner limit.\n\nA co-ordinated raid is developing on your sector and tracks are already held at the sector edge. Hostile intent has been assessed for the sector as a whole, but identification remains track by track. Nothing may be fired on unless it is classified Enemy. Any track presenting as Unknown must be referred to the commander for classification; expect an answer in about fifteen seconds, and continue servicing confirmed hostiles while you wait. Some referrals may not come back.\n\nYou hold thirteen rounds across three launcher types and a hard system limit of two rockets in the air at once. A third engagement cannot begin until one of the two in flight resolves as hit, kill or miss. Friendly and civil movement is expected in the sector. You will not have enough rounds or enough launcher time to service everything comfortably — sequence accordingly.",
